From 72c5261d0534308daa5173f3600e7e7dc86ad89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:09:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: copy the real url view and the favicon clip into the
 tab sheet close hand-off

During the closing cross-fade the url text in the pill still doubled
toward the end (the first glyph and baseline lined up, the rest drifted a
couple of pixels), and the favicon copy was a square where the real
favicon is a circle.

The text copy was laid out again by the pill's own text views and moved
to meet the first glyph and baseline of the real url text. Its width,
end, ellipsis, fading edge and scroll are not the real view's, so two
layouts of one string that start at the same pixel end at different
ones. The favicon is a circle because its view clips to an oval outline,
and a clip to an outline is applied only when the compositor draws the
view. The icon copy is a bitmap drawn with View.draw into a software
canvas, which does not apply it, so the copy kept its square corners.

On a hand-off that read the live bar, the real url view is now copied as
one bitmap and shown over the real one, at its size and place and with
the hand-off alpha. The canvas is shifted by the view's scroll first, as
its parent does, so a scrolled url bar is copied as it is shown. The
pill's own text is drawn at alpha 0 while that bitmap is up and stays as
the fallback if no copy could be made. The bitmap is hidden and freed
when the fade ends or the sheet opens again. Taking it down in a layout
frame needs nothing more, because the pill's text is given its alphas
every frame before the bitmap clears them. A teardown with no frame of
its own (the sheet being destroyed) gives the label its alpha back where
the bitmap is cleared away. An icon copy now takes the clip of its real
view (the real provider, asked on the copy so a circle stays a circle,
with no outline alpha so the copy casts no shadow), and drops it when it
is reused for an icon that has none. A copy that cannot be drawn into a
bitmap falls back on any RuntimeException.

The 130 ms fade, the bar band, the page and top toolbar restore, the
open path, the spring and the copies' sizes before the hand-off are
unchanged. The unit tests cover the url bitmap's size, place, end and
fade, its scroll, its removal at the end of the fade, on a reopen (the
first frame after it is the bar itself, the next is the settled pill)
and on a teardown, the fallback when the live bar is not read, and the
circular clip of the favicon copy in the hand-off, while the pill
travels, and when the copy is reused.
